k out in March.', true, 'billing', 2, 'en'),
  (104, 'Could you please check what went wrong, cancel the incorrect invoices, and send us one corrected invoice for the twelve seats at the team price that we actually ordered? If an amount was already collected by direct debit for the wrong invoices, we expect the difference to be credited back to our account before the end of the month. We have been happy customers for two years and would like to keep it that way, but this situation has cost our team several hours already and our CFO is asking whether we should look at other vendors. Please also let us know whether the logout problem is a known issue and when a fix can be expected, because the workaround suggested in your help center does not work for us. Thank you in advance for a quick reply; you can reach me by email or by phone during business hours. Hello support team, I am writing on behalf of our finance department about the subscription we took out in March. Since then we have received three invoices for the same period, each with a slightly different amount, and our accountant cannot reconcile them with the bank statements. The first invoice listed twelve seats at the team price, the second one fourteen seats at the enterprise price, and the third one again twelve seats but with an additional charge for premium support that we never ordered. We tried to change the billing contact in the portal last week, but the page shows an error and the old contact keeps receiving all the emails, including the payment reminders. Our procurement policy requires that every invoice matches the purchase order exactly, so at the moment none of these invoices can be approved and your system keeps sending reminders that payment is overdue. In addition, two of our users report that the desktop application logs them out several times per hour since the latest update, which makes it very hard to finish the monthly reports on time. I have attached the purchase order and the three invoices to this message so that you can compare